This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

The user is building a cabinet-making application from scratch (a prior attempt failed due to measurement system problems). The primary deliverable is a living project plan at `/workspace/docs/project-cabinet-maker.md`. The user has been iteratively expanding the plan through conversation, answering architectural questions and adding requirements. The core requests, in order, were:

- Create a detailed project plan for a C# Blazor .NET 10, EF Core, Bootstrap app for cabinet/furniture measurement management
- Add multi-tenancy with role-based security groups (SystemAdmin, TenantAdmin, TenantUser)
- Answer infrastructure questions: Docker/Linux deployment, MySQL primary/SQL Server secondary, Excel export (ClosedXML), system base material library + tenant delta overrides in `MaterialTenantDetails`
- Design a full temporal succession pattern for material pricing/attributes (EffectiveDate/ObsoleteDate shared boundary)
- Handle timezone architecture: `DateTime` UTC always, UI converts via NodaTime, DST gap/overlap disambiguation
- Change all table PKs from `Guid` to `int {TableName}Id`, keep `Guid {TableName}Guid` for UI references only
- Document self-signup auto-creating a personal `Tenant` (TenantId null only for SystemAdmin)
- Add subscription plans (Solo/Team) as `CmType` dictionary entries, with `IPlanGateService` and `<PlanGate>` Blazor component
- Align plan with actual base classes `CmEntity` / `CmEntityHistory` (not a fictional `BaseEntity`); keep `DateTime` not `DateTimeOffset`
- Use injected `TimeProvider` instead of `DateTime.UtcNow` directly: `_timeProvider.GetUtcNow().DateTime`
- **Most recent**: Introduce `CabinetMaker.Domain.Shared` project for shared POCOs, repository interfaces, Result<T>, and Mapperly mappers; `Domain` stays private to DAL only

2. Key Technical Concepts:

- **C# Blazor Server .NET 10** — Interactive Server render mode, `@rendermode InteractiveServer`
- **Entity Framework Core 10** — MySQL (Pomelo) primary, SQL Server secondary; provider switching via `DatabaseProviderExtensions`; Global Query Filters for tenant isolation and soft deletes; `SaveChangesAsync` override for auto-stamp TenantId and Guid generation
- **MySQL `DATETIME` type** — explicitly NOT `TIMESTAMP` (avoids server timezone auto-conversion)
- **Multi-tenancy** — row-level isolation, `ITenantScoped` interface (`int TenantId`), Global Query Filter, `ITenantContext` reads `tenant_id` int claim
- **Key naming convention** — `int {TableName}Id` (PK, internal joins only), `Guid {TableName}Guid` (UI/external), server-generated on insert
- **`CmEntity` / `CmEntityHistory`** — actual base classes in `CabinetMaker.Domain.Entities`; `CmEntity` has `CreatedDate`, `CreatedUserId`, `LastUpdatedDate`, `LastUpdatedUserId`, `RecordStateId`; `CmEntityHistory` extends with `EffectiveDate`, `ObsoleteDate` (both `DateTime`)
- **DateTime UTC convention** — `DateTime` always UTC; `TimeProvider` injected; `_timeProvider.GetUtcNow().DateTime` is the only permitted "now" source; EF global value converter enforces `DateTimeKind.Utc`
- **`TimeProvider`** — .NET 8+ abstraction; `TimeProvider.System` registered as singleton in DI; `FakeTimeProvider` (`Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing`) for tests
- **Temporal succession pattern** — `ObsoleteDate(outgoing) == EffectiveDate(incoming)`, shared boundary, no gap/no overlap; `RecordSuccessionService` is the only write path; supports future-dating
- **DST handling** — NodaTime `ZoneLocalMapping.Count`: 0=gap (spring forward, `SkippedTimeException`), 2=overlap (fall back, `AmbiguousTimeException`); `DateTimeInput` component handles disambiguation; UTC-stored succession records are DST-immune
- **Material library two-tier model** — `Material` (system, not tenant-scoped) + `MaterialDetail`/`MaterialAttribute`; `MaterialTenantDetail`/`MaterialTenantAttribute` (tenant delta overrides, `CmEntityHistory`-based); `MaterialResolutionService` with `asOfDate` parameter; delta-only (null=inherit system)
- **System dictionary pattern** — `CmTypeClass` / `CmType` parent-child; all enums/states as `CmType` records; plan types, record states, operation types all seeded as `CmType` data
- **MVVM** — `CommunityToolkit.Mvvm`; `[ObservableProperty]`, `[RelayCommand]`; `ViewModelComponentBase<T>` bridges `PropertyChanged` → `StateHasChanged()`
- **CommunityToolkit.Mvvm** — source generator-based MVVM
- **Subscription plans** — `PlanTypeId` on `Tenant` FK to `CmType`; `IPlanGateService` reads `tenant_plan` claim; `<PlanGate>` Blazor component; downgrade blocked if multiple active users
- **`RegistrationService`** — atomically creates `ApplicationUser` + `Tenant` (Solo plan) + assigns TenantAdmin role
- **`Domain.Shared` project** — POCOs, repository interfaces (returning POCOs), `Result<T>`, enums, Mapperly POCO→POCO mappers; no EF dependency
- **Mapperly (`Riok.Mapperly`)** — source generator mapper; `[Mapper]` attribute on partial class; Entity→POCO mappers in DAL; POCO→POCO in Domain.Shared; `PrivateAssets="all"` NuGet reference (no runtime DLL)
- **Docker/Linux** — multi-stage Dockerfile (`mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/sdk:10.0` build, `mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:10.0-bookworm-slim` runtime); docker-compose with web + MySQL containers; all config via env vars
- **ClosedXML** — Excel export for cut lists and material estimates
- **NodaTime** — IANA timezone conversions in Web layer only; `DateTimeZoneProviders.Tzdb`
- **FluentValidation** — entity/command validation in BRL
- **`Result<T>`** — discriminated union (success/failure) returned by all BRL services

3. Files and Code Sections:

- **`/workspace/docs/project-cabinet-maker.md`** — Primary deliverable. ~900+ lines. Contains 13 numbered sections, 18 architecture decisions (D1-D18), 13 open questions (several answered). Last edit added the Domain.Shared architecture to Section 3.

- **`/workspace/src/CabinetMaker.Domain/Entities/CmEntity.cs`** — Read to understand actual base class. User had already fixed typo and casing. Current state:
  ```csharp
  namespace CabinetMaker.Domain.Entities;
  public class CmEntity
  {
      public DateTime CreatedDate { get; set; }
      public int CreatedUserId { get; set; }
      public DateTime? LastUpdatedDate { get; set; }
      public int? LastUpdatedUserId { get; set; }
      public int RecordStateId { get; set; }
  }
  ```

- **`/workspace/src/CabinetMaker.Domain/Entities/CmEntityHistory.cs`** — Read to understand temporal base class. Current state:
  ```csharp
  namespace CabinetMaker.Domain.Entities;
  public class CmEntityHistory : CmEntity
  {
      public DateTime EffectiveDate { get; set; }
      public DateTime? ObsoleteDate { get; set; }
  }
  ```

- **`/workspace/CabinetMaker.slnx`** — Read. Currently has 3 solution folders: `/10-Servers/` (Web), `/20-BusinessRules/` (BRL), `/30-Data Layer/` (DAL + Domain). `Domain.Shared` has NOT yet been added.

- **`/workspace/src/CabinetMaker.Web/CabinetMaker.Web.csproj`** — Read. Blazor Server .NET 10, `BlazorDisableThrowNavigationException=true`.

- **`/workspace/src/CabinetMaker.DAL/CabinetMaker.DAL.csproj`** — Read. Has EF Core, SQL Server provider, ASP.NET Identity EF packages.

- **`/workspace/src/CabinetMaker.Domain/CabinetMaker.Domain.csproj`** — Read. Has `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Abstractions`.

Key entity schemas now in plan (all use `CmEntity` or `CmEntityHistory` base, `int {Name}Id` PK, `Guid {Name}Guid`):

```csharp
// Tenant entity
public class Tenant : CmEntity  // NOT ITenantScoped
{
    public int TenantId { get; set; }
    public Guid TenantGuid { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Slug { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public bool IsActive { get; set; } = true;
    public int PlanTypeId { get; set; }       // FK → CmType (Solo/Team)
    public virtual CmType PlanType { get; set; } = null!;
    public int? MeasurementPreferenceId { get; set; }
    public virtual ICollection<ApplicationUser> Users { get; set; }
}

// ApplicationUser (Identity exception to naming convention)
public class ApplicationUser : IdentityUser<int>
{
    public Guid UserGuid { get; set; }
    public int? TenantId { get; set; }   // null = SystemAdmin
    public string DisplayName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string TimeZoneId { get; set; } = "UTC";
    public int? MeasurementPreferenceId { get; set; }
}

// ITenantScoped (int, not Guid)
public interface ITenantScoped
{
    int TenantId { get; set; }
}

// ITemporalRecord (matches CmEntityHistory)
public interface ITemporalRecord
{
    DateTime EffectiveDate { get; set; }
    DateTime? ObsoleteDate { get; set; }
}

// MaterialTenantDetail
public class MaterialTenantDetail : CmEntityHistory, ITenantScoped
{
    public int MaterialTenantDetailId { get; set; }
    public Guid MaterialTenantDetailGuid { get; set; }
    public int TenantId { get; set; }
    public int MaterialId { get; set; }
    public bool IsHidden { get; set; }
